<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thibaw Min</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1859">1859</a>–<a href="/years/1916">1916</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Thibaw</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thibaw Min was the last king of the Konbaung dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, reigning from 1878 to 1885. His reign began with the killing of many royal relatives and faced revolts among the Shan states, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limbin-confederacy">Limbin Confederacy</a>. A dispute over a British teak company led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-anglo-burmese-war">Third Anglo-Burmese War</a> of 1885, after which he was exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratnagiri">Ratnagiri</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thibaw-min.jpg" alt="Thibaw Min" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thibaw_Min.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His successor <b>Thibaw</b> (r. 1878–1885) was placed on the throne by a palace faction led by the queen Hsinbyumashin and her daughter Supayalat, and the execution of dozens of royal relatives in 1879 damaged his reputation in Britain.</blockquote><a href="/empire/konbaung-dynasty">Konbaung dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Hsipaw, Shan <b>Thibaw</b>, was founded as a Shan principality in the Dokhtawady valley of the northern Shan plateau; tradition dates its ruling house to the 14th century.</blockquote><a href="/state/hsipaw-state">Hsipaw State</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 1880s the Mongnai saopha joined the Limbin Confederacy against <b>King Thibaw</b> and then the British, but submitted in 1887.</blockquote><a href="/state/mongnai-state">Mongnai State</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandalay">Mandalay</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratnagiri">Ratnagiri</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=21.98,96.08&amp;year=1896" aria-label="Mandalay on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7126 1352 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Thibaw Min"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7576 1622h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7576 1622h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=21.98,96.08&amp;year=1896">What was here in 1896? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
